    "title": "Every member, or one by one",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-reduplicated-classifiers-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Every member, or one by one",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "A repeated classifier such as 个个 means every member of a known group, often followed by 都. Repeating a number-and-classifier phrase, as in 一件一件地, instead describes doing an action to items one by one. The story uses this second pattern.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "这些人个个都很高。",
                "pinyin": "zhèxiē rén gè gè dōu hěn gāo 。",
                "meaning": "Every one of these people is tall.",
                "audio": "c720b8967c69228b589b644cf5f947525aa0c977d9824bcb9e45b4bae09819d4"
              },
              {
                "text": "我一件一件地看大衣。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ yī jiàn yī jiàn de kàn dàyī 。",
                "meaning": "I look at the coats one by one.",
                "audio": "c567c055a88e22b566c7f8e577703a2268bc7ff64c59e220673c4444a2f44d52"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "个",
                "pinyin": "gè",
                "meaning": "general measure word",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "1f3f9d4727cf55cddd76e8ee909c91776237923957a4f0b77e0ce352fbc0e91e"
              },
              {
                "text": "张",
                "pinyin": "zhāng",
                "meaning": "measure word for flat objects",
                "singleWord": true,
